{
  "sticker": "deer",
  "called": "the fawn",
  "skeleton": "four-legged fawn standing, three-quarter view facing left: root on the ground; body with neck (belly squash on the body); head on the neck, face with eyes and mouth; earL/earR on the head (flick); four slender legs at shoulders and hips (far ones behind, shaded); little tail at the rump (wags).",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a fawn character. Draw this exact fawn as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the body: the spotted fawn body with its neck and chest, white spots on the back, as in image 1, without head, without tail and without any legs: no legs, no shoulders, no thighs and no haunches drawn on it — its underside one smooth rounded line from the chest to the rump; the top of the neck, normally under the head, rounded.\n2. the head: the fawn's head with its black nose, facing left as in image 1, with a completely blank face — no eyes, no mouth — keep the nose and the rosy cheek; without ears and without any neck: the head ends at the chin and jaw, its bottom edge the smooth rounded line of the jaw and the back of the head, nothing hanging below it.\n3. one ear: a big pointed ear with its pink inside, as the ear on the right of image 1, with a rounded base.\n4. one front leg: the near front leg of image 1 drawn whole, from the top of the shoulder down to the hoof: the broad rounded shoulder and upper leg (the part that joins the chest), tapering into the slender lower leg and its dark hoof; its top is the full, smooth, rounded curve of the shoulder.\n5. one back leg: the near back leg of image 1 drawn whole, from the top of the haunch down to the hoof: the big rounded thigh (the whole haunch at the rump, as big as it is in image 1), the bent hock, the slender lower leg and its dark hoof; its top is the full, smooth, rounded curve of the haunch.\n6. the tail: the little white fluffy tail, with a rounded base.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a fawn character; image 2 shows the same fawn cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the fawn's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the fawn in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the fawn's left eye (on the right of image 1) as it is in image 1: a big dark round eye with a white sparkle.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the mouth as it is in image 1: a small happy smile.\n7. the mouth wide open in a big happy laugh, the inside pink.\n8. the mouth open in a small round 'o'.\n9. the mouth in a small sad frown.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    }
  ],
